wifi: mt76: compat: Linux 7.3 allocator and mac80211 helpers on older hosts

Four constructs in the Linux 7.3 mt76 sources need helpers that older hosts do
not have:

  - kzalloc_flex() and kzalloc_obj(), which 6.17 hosts lack (6.18 and later
    stable kernels have them) and which the new regd.c allocations and
    mt7925_mac_sta_add() use. They
    expand to kzalloc(struct_size(...), GFP_KERNEL) and
    kzalloc(sizeof(*p), GFP_KERNEL), so those calls use the plain form, which
    is valid everywhere.
  - ieee80211_txq_aql_pending(), a Linux 7.2 mac80211 helper that mt76's power
    save buffering consults. Kbuild defines MT76_NO_AQL_PENDING when the host's
    mac80211.h lacks it, and the check is then skipped, which is what hosts
    without the accounting did before.
  - ieee80211_nan_cluster_joined(), also Linux 7.2, called when the NAN firmware
    reports a cluster join. Kbuild defines MT76_NO_NAN_CLUSTER_JOINED when it is
    missing, and the notification is then not sent.

Kbuild tests for the symbol in the host headers, not the kernel version, so a
distro kernel that backported one keeps using it.

--- a/mt7925/regd.c
+++ b/mt7925/regd.c
@@ -336,7 +336,7 @@
 		goto err;
 	}
 
-	regd = kzalloc_flex(*regd, reg_rules, num_of_rules);
+	regd = kzalloc(struct_size(regd, reg_rules, num_of_rules), GFP_KERNEL);
 	if (!regd) {
 		ret = -ENOMEM;
 		goto err;
